    "The actual resident-store release increments its epoch and clears old metadata while outstanding MTP sources keep original device allocations alive.",
    "A new model can obtain independent storage while old sources retire. The final owner frees each original allocation once.",
    "Raw shard replacement rejects an adopted native MTP model owner. Ordinary unleased release remains covered by the original Windows host harness."
